    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSpacious 4-bedroom detached residence on a generous c.0.56 acre site with full basement & attic conversion potential\n\nDNG Ted Healy are delighted to present this attractive four-bedroom property, ideally positioned at Knockmanagh, Tiernaboul, just approximately 7km from Killarney town.\n\nSet on a generous 0.56-acre site, this property offers an excellent combination of space, privacy and potential, making it an ideal choice for families seeking a substantial home within easy reach of Killarney, while also offering considerable scope for future enhancement.\n\nThe property comprises a four-bedroom detached residence extending over a full basement, providing valuable additional space and excellent flexibility for a variety of uses. Another attractive feature is the attic space, which is ready for full conversion, subject to the necessary planning permissions and building regulations. This offers the opportunity to significantly increase the overall accommodation and create additional bedrooms, home office space, games room or other living accommodation to suit individual requirements.\n\nThe property itself provides well-proportioned accommodation at ground-floor level, with the generous site adding to the property's appeal. The full basement is an important additional feature, offering substantial storage and ancillary space and providing further possibilities for the new owner.\n\nThe surrounding countryside provides a peaceful residential setting, while the property remains conveniently located for everyday amenities and services. Tiernaboul National School is just over 2km away, making this an especially appealing location for families with young children. Killarney town, approximately 7km away, offers an extensive range of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and services, together with easy access to the wider road network.\n\nThe property is also ideally placed to enjoy all that the Killarney area has to offer, including Killarney National Park, the Lakes of Killarney and the many outdoor recreational amenities associated with the area."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.07m x 1.76m\nSolid Timber floor\n\nLiving Room - 4.15m x 4.86m\nSolid timber flooring, solid burning stove with wooden surround, double doors to kitchen\n\nKitchen - 4.29m x 6.25m\nFloor and eye level fitted kitchen units with integrated oven, hob & extractor, tiled backsplash, solid timber floor, patio door\n\nHallway - 5.75m x 1.14m\nSolid timber floor\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.82m x 4.42m\nSolid timber floor\n\nEn Suite - 1.5m x 1.95m\nWC, WHB, shower, tiled\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.31m x 3.61m\nSolid timber floor\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.83m x 3.5m\nSolid timber floor\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.3m x 2.91m\nSolid timber floor\n\nBathroom - 3.3m x 1.71m\nTiled, WC, WHB, Bath\n\nBasement 1 - 8.6m x 4.1m\nLarge open basement storage area\n\nBasement 2 - 8.58m x 10.61\nLarge open basement storage area, oil boiler\n\nAttic - 15m x 4.32m\nLarge attic with gable windows installed\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
